---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import MarketingChrome from "../../components/MarketingChrome.astro";

const phoneDisplay = "(501) 413-3386";
const tel = "tel:+15014133386";
const sms = "sms:+15014133386";
---

<Base
  title='Websites for Panaderías and Mexican Bakeries | NV Labs'
  description='A free demo website for your panadería, in English and Spanish. Pan dulce, tres leches, quinceañera cakes. Call or text (501) 413-3386.'
  image="/og.png"
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <MarketingChrome>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Panaderías and Mexican bakeries</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">A website for your panadería, in English and Spanish</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A free demo site that shows your pan dulce, cakes, hours, and how to order. Built so both
        Spanish and English customers can find what they need.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text me</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="search-title">
      <h2 id="search-title">People are searching for pan dulce near them</h2>
      <p>
        When someone wants fresh conchas on a Sunday morning, they pull out their phone and search.
        Some type "Mexican bakery near me." Others type "panadería cerca de mí." Your website
        should show up for both.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="lang-title">
      <h2 id="lang-title">Two languages, one simple site</h2>
      <p>
        A lot of your regulars might be more comfortable in Spanish. Plenty of new customers might
        only read English. I suggest building your site in both, with a simple button to switch.
      </p>
      <p>
        That way abuela can read the cake menu, and her grandkid's friend who just moved to the
        neighborhood can too. If you'd rather keep it to one language, that's fine. It's your call.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="bake-title">
      <h2 id="bake-title">Show off what you bake</h2>
      <p>Your case is full of things people love but might not know the names of. I'll lay it out so it's easy to browse:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pan dulce:</strong> conchas, orejas, cuernos, marranitos, polvorones, and whatever else you make</li>
        <li><strong>Cakes:</strong> tres leches, chocolate, fruit cakes, and your house specials</li>
        <li><strong>Seasonal items:</strong> rosca de reyes, pan de muerto, tamales if you sell them</li>
        <li><strong>Drinks:</strong> champurrado, café de olla, or whatever you serve with it</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cele-title">
      <h2 id="cele-title">Quinceañera, birthday, and wedding cakes</h2>
      <p>
        Celebration cakes are a big part of a panadería's business. Families plan these for weeks.
        I'll set up a page that shows photos of cakes you've made and a simple order request form
        for the date, number of people, flavors, and colors.
      </p>
      <p>
        Requests come straight to your phone or email, in whichever language the customer wrote.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="expect-title">
      <h2 id="expect-title">Hours, address, and what to expect</h2>
      <p>
        Some panaderías sell out early. Some only take cash. Some have a parking lot around back.
        I'll put all of that right up front so customers come in prepared and happy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="free-title">
      <h2 id="free-title">Free demo, no commitment</h2>
      <p>
        I build your demo first. You look at it and decide. If it feels right, I put it live. If
        not, you don't owe me anything.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <h2 id="faq-title">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div>
          <h3>Can you write the Spanish part of the site?</h3>
          <p>
            Yes, I can prepare the Spanish text, and I'll always have you look it over so it sounds
            the way you and your customers talk. You know your community best.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Do I need photos of every pan?</h3>
          <p>
            No. A handful of good photos of your case and a few celebration cakes go a long way. We
            can add more over time.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Can customers order a quinceañera cake through the site?</h3>
          <p>
            They can send an order request with all the details. You review it and confirm by phone
            or text, just like you do now, only with less back and forth.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
      <h2 id="cta-title">¿Listo para ver su página? Ready to see your site?</h2>
      <p>Hablo con usted por teléfono o texto. Let's build your demo.</p>
      <a class="phone-big" href={tel}>{phoneDisplay}</a>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text</a>
      </div>
      <a class="back-home" href="/">Back to NV Labs home</a>
    </section>
  </MarketingChrome>
</Base>
